<title>FRANCE: French September trade surplus 10.09 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French September trade surplus 10.09 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in September of 10.09 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in August of 13.37 billion, provisional customs office data showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus of 13.89 billion francs for August.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  Sept     Aug</p>
<p> Trade balance			10.09    13.37</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)	8.60     7.53</p>
<p> Imports			     114.44   112.25</p>
<p> Exports			     124.53   125.62</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     5.00     5.38</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -6.18    -5.16</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance     7.12     9.03</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 2.33 (6 planes)  2.14 (6)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     1.10    2.18</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		123.30   92.51</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		114.69   84.98</p>
<p> European Union			4.99    2.29</p>
<p> Germany				 0.11    1.18</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.68   -1.51</p>
<p> United States			-2.53    0.55</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first three months of the year were as follows</p>
<p>				    Jan-Sept 1996     Jan-Sept 1995</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment    84.98		69.83</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	     86.76		72.32</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
